A Token Bucket rate limiter regulates request traffic by adding tokens to a bucket at a constant refill rate up to a maximum burst capacity. Below is an efficient, production-ready in-memory implementation in TypeScript:

```typescript
export class TokenBucketRateLimiter {
  private capacity: number;
  private refillRatePerSecond: number;
  private tokens: number;
  private lastRefillTimestamp: number;

  constructor(capacity: number, refillRatePerSecond: number) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.refillRatePerSecond = refillRatePerSecond;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefillTimestamp = Date.now();
  }

  private refill(): void {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsedSeconds = (now - this.lastRefillTimestamp) / 1000;
    const tokensToAdd = elapsedSeconds * this.refillRatePerSecond;

    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + tokensToAdd);
    this.lastRefillTimestamp = now;
  }

  public tryConsume(tokensToConsume = 1): boolean {
    this.refill();

    if (this.tokens >= tokensToConsume) {
      this.tokens -= tokensToConsume;
      return true;
    }

    return false;
  }

  public getRemainingTokens(): number {
    this.refill();
    return Math.floor(this.tokens);
  }
}
```

Usage Example:
```typescript
// Allow up to 10 requests burst, refilling at 2 requests per second
const limiter = new TokenBucketRateLimiter(10, 2);

if (limiter.tryConsume(1)) {
  // Process API request
} else {
  // Return 429 Too Many Requests
}
```

Key Technical Attributes:
- O(1) time complexity per check.
- Zero background timers or setInterval leaks; tokens are calculated lazily on demand.
- Handles fractional token replenishment smoothly.
